Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper, A View From Somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.73,0:00:07.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}published at ICLR 2023 by researchers at Sony AI and the University of Tokyo,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.78,0:00:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rethinks how we represent human faces in datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.06,0:00:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Instead of relying on problematic demographic labels like race or gender,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.85,0:00:21.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors collect over six hundred thousand human judgments of face similarity and learn
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.76,0:00:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a continuous embedding space aligned with human perception.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.63,0:00:29.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The result is a face representation that is interpretable,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.44,0:00:33.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that avoids invasive categorical labels, and that captures the smooth,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.03,0:00:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}continuous nature of human phenotypic diversity,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.18,0:00:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}opening a new path for measuring dataset diversity more responsibly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.94,0:00:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Evaluating the diversity of face datasets almost always relies on categorical demographic labels such as race,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.39,0:00:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gender, or age.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.85,0:00:55.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}But these labels are frequently unavailable, legally restricted to collect,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.30,0:00:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and prone to bias when they are inferred by annotators rather than self-reported.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.75,0:01:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Worse,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.21,0:01:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}categorical labels flatten the continuous nature of human appearance: skin tone becomes simply light or dark,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.66,0:01:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and two faces sharing the same label can still look strikingly different.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.11,0:01:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rigid taxonomies also erase multi-ethnic people, shift meaning across cultures,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.57,0:01:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and can cause real psychological harm when someone is mislabeled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.32,0:01:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors argue that face similarity is fundamentally continuous and depends on who is doing the judging.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.85,0:01:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}If we could learn a representation directly aligned with human perception,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.37,0:01:38.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}we could sidestep problematic semantic labels entirely while still measuring diversity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.68,0:01:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Existing psychological-embedding methods fall short: they either cannot embed new faces beyond the fixed training set,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.88,0:01:48.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or they pool every judgment together,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.14,0:01:53.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}throwing away the meaningful differences within and between individual annotators.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.44,0:01:57.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Their answer is A View From Somewhere, or AVFS.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.40,0:02:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They collect a dataset of six hundred thirty-eight thousand triplet similarity judgments
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.37,0:02:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}over nearly five thousand faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.33,0:02:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and crucially,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.29,0:02:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}each judgment records the identity and self-reported demographics of the annotator who made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.25,0:02:17.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On top of this data they build a conditional learning framework that produces a continuous,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.22,0:02:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}low-dimensional, and human-interpretable embedding space,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.18,0:02:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}along with per-annotator masks that reveal how different people weigh different visual dimensions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.44,0:02:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}At the core is a conditional convolutional network, a ResNet eighteen,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.83,0:02:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that maps each face to a one-hundred-twenty-eight-dimensional embedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.35,0:02:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training uses odd-one-out judgments: given a triplet of faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.25,0:02:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an annotator picks the least similar one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.82,0:02:45.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each annotator is assigned a learnable gating mask, passed through a sigmoid,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.65,0:02:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}that scales the importance of every embedding dimension for that person.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.17,0:02:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Similarity between two faces is the dot product of their masked,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.19,0:02:55.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rectified embeddings,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.51,0:03:01.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and the model predicts the odd-one-out probability directly from these three pairwise similarities.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.72,0:03:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A sparsity and non-negativity penalty keeps the dimensions few and interpretable,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.81,0:03:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}leaving only about twenty-two active dimensions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.12,0:03:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The AVFS dataset comprises six hundred thirty-eight thousand quality-controlled triplet
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.74,0:03:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}judgments over four thousand nine hundred twenty-one near-frontal face images.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.78,0:03:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Every single judgment carries the annotator's identifier and self-identified demographic attributes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.23,0:03:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors evaluate on held-out judgments over the same stimuli,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.43,0:03:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on eighty thousand judgments over entirely novel faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.98,0:03:40.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and against attribute-recognition baselines trained on CelebA and FairFace semantic labels.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.16,0:03:45.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Across both the same-stimuli and the novel-stimuli evaluations,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.42,0:03:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the AVFS models predict human similarity judgments more accurately than baselines trained on semantic labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.68,0:03:53.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and they better capture the uncertainty in human judgments as measured by Spearman correlation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.95,0:03:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.21,0:04:02.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the annotator-specific masks generalize even to triplets made entirely of novel,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.47,0:04:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}previously unseen faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.73,0:04:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which shows the embedding space is far more closely aligned with the human mental representation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.00,0:04:15.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}of faces than spaces learned from rigid categorical labels.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.56,0:04:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To test whether annotators really matter,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.08,0:04:23.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors randomly shuffle which annotator mask is attached to each of the eighty thousand
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.73,0:04:26.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}judgments and recompute accuracy a hundred times over.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.05,0:04:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Accuracy drops from about sixty-two percent down to roughly fifty-three percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.97,0:04:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}proving that annotators are genuinely not interchangeable.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.53,0:04:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A dimension-elimination analysis further shows that only six to thirteen dimensions are
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.88,0:04:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}needed to recover most of the predictive accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.95,0:04:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while fifteen to twenty-two dimensions are required to explain the full similarity structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.66,0:04:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}clear evidence that similarity is context-dependent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.16,0:04:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline numbers tell the whole story.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.81,0:05:03.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Six hundred thirty-eight thousand human judgments gathered over four thousand nine hundred twenty-one distinct faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.20,0:05:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Twenty-two interpretable embedding dimensions retained at nearly sixty-two percent validation accuracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.71,0:05:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And when annotator identities are scrambled,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.49,0:05:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}accuracy falls from sixty-one point seven down to fifty-two point eight percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.54,0:05:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all achieved without ever training on a single semantic label.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.76,0:05:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The key takeaway is that learning face representations from human similarity judgments,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.09,0:05:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instead of demographic labels, produces a continuous, interpretable,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.25,0:05:37.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and perception-aligned embedding space that supports diversity analysis without invasive categorical labeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.98,0:05:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And because the framework only requires keeping track of which annotator made which judgment,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.67,0:05:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the same conditional approach can extend naturally to almost any machine-learning task
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.94,0:05:51.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}built on subjective human decisions.
